{
  "text": "Today, we'll see Insight Gen investigate a real business question on Blue Orbit. Then we'll go under the hood, how business expertise, connected components, and continuous improvement make it work at Amex. This is Insight Gen, the insight generation agent in Blue Orbit. We start by creating a workspace and enabling Lumi MCP and analytical skills. We ask for a year- over- year comparison of Dollar C 60 trends for Charge and Lend. Before proceeding, the agent clarifies the methodology, metric, and analytical depth. It consults the governed knowledge bundle for metric definitions, calculation rules, and source tables before querying the data and running the analysis. The report opens with key findings and a like- for- like comparison. Both products show modest improvement. Linked references open business definitions directly in the governed knowledge bundle. Interactive previews make the monthly patterns easy to inspect, with separate views for Charge and Lend and clear year- over- year comparisons. The supporting SQL, data extracts, and charts are linked alongside the report, so we can inspect the underlying evidence. Next, we ask what might explain the second quarter improvement. InsightGen ranks candidate hypotheses, spelling out their mechanisms, expected signals, and tests, rather than jumping straight to a conclusion. We ask it to test the top two. The results reject favorable portfolio mix as the explanation and find repayment behavior supportive for Charge but not Lend. Finally, InsightGen brings the investigation together: an executive summary, decisive charts, supporting evidence, and recommended next steps. Now, let's see how we make this work in the Amex business setting. General purpose agents bring reasoning and tools. Our differentiator is the enterprise system around them: business owned knowledge, reusable expert methods, controlled data access, and evidence driven improvement. Business teams curate definitions, policies, and context in Enterprise Knowledge Foundation. Their analytical expertise becomes reusable primitives and skills through Skill Foundry. The C 60 definition grounds comparison, segmentation, and testing. Those primitives compose into a governed skill with its source links retained. Teams use Insight Gen to apply that knowledge and skill, connect to permitted data, and return findings with evidence. As the agent runs, the agent observability framework captures its execution trace and quality signals. Harness Intelligence uses the evidence to diagnose, test, and validate a change. The improved skill returns to Skill Foundry and the next agent run. Built once, specialized many times, improving continuously.",
